## Context
Minor (`verifiable:`) findings from the 2026-06-11 prose review panel, batched
for one editorial pass. Majors are tickets 0531/0532/0533. Imagine-phase
triage (2026-06-11) verified each item against the current text; line numbers
below are anchors as of origin/main 522fc29e and will shift after 0532/0533
land — re-locate by quoted text, not line number.

Sequencing: runs LAST, on top of 0533 (lines ~97–103 region) and 0532
(abstract/conclusion). Items 1 and 4 sit in 0533's footprint — re-read the
post-0533 text before editing.

## Actions (one pass over slides/manuscript/main.md)
1. Status accuracy stratum (~l.99): the mechanical explanation (38% proposed
   rows have no admissible label) is already in the prose; confirm it states
   the caveat clearly. Add the accuracy-excluding-proposed number ONLY if it
   derives from a committed artifact (0531 macros not shipped); otherwise
   waive the number with a one-line reason.
2. PyPSA-ASEAN (~l.37): add a citation if a refs.bib entry exists or can be
   added with real bibliographic data; otherwise mark "(in preparation)" /
   URL note. House rule: no in-repo documents in the bibliography.
3. "More than doubles recall" (~l.162): pin the denominator in the headline
   sentence — "more than doubles recall relative to the single-run mean
   (2.4x)"; the best-single-run comparison is already disclosed in the body.
4. Two 73% figures (caption ~l.103 vs pipeline-aggregate ~l.97): disambiguate
   the figure caption to "73% light-reviewed Wikipedia coverage of all 177
   plants (130/177)". OVERLAP: 0533 edits this region — re-read first.
5. Cross-experiment baseline (~l.388 annex vs §Exp2 body): add one clarifying
   sentence in the Exp2 body that the naive arm is an independent sweep, not
   directly comparable to Exp1 parametric scores; within-Exp2 comparisons use
   the common arm-1 sweep.
6. rapidfuzz false-match estimate: WAIVE — no committed artifact supports a
   validated estimate; the concordance table already carries the upper-bound
   caveat. Log the waiver.
7. "Characterised in earlier in-project work" (~l.325): replace with a
   within-document pointer to the interday/top-up characterisation sub-section
   (~l.333) — same annex, removes the uncited vague reference.
8. AI-tells: verb "leverage" (~l.79) → e.g. "exploit"; noun "The leverage"
   (~l.156) → e.g. "The value"; "energy landscape" (~l.37) and "empirical
   landscape" (~l.39) → plain alternatives. DO NOT touch section headings
   containing "landscape" (~l.49, ~l.75) — crossref labels are frozen
   (tests/test_manuscript_crossref.py).
9. Prose nits: "takes a problem" (~l.59) → "addresses a problem"; double
   "To our knowledge" (~l.160) → merge or reword the second occurrence.
10. Interday drift (~l.333): add one limitation sentence naming provider-side
    silent movement (observed up to ΔF1=0.289/24h, qwen3.6-27b) as
    unquantified interday variance beyond the 5-rep within-session spread.
    Number already in the manuscript/artifacts — no new derivation.
11. Cohort naming: first-use disambiguation exists (~l.93); sweep for orphan
    uses of "14-model analysis cohort" lacking the cohort qualifier or
    back-ref; add the parenthetical where missing.
12. Mistral branding (~l.314): verified against models.yaml display_name
    (Small 4 / Medium 3.5 / Large 3) — matches; confirm in log, no edit.
13. config/ai-tells.yml: WAIVE — YAGNI tooling inside a manuscript editorial
    ticket; item-8 instances are fixed directly. A reusable scanner, if ever
    wanted, is a separate chore ticket. Log the waiver.

## Invariants
- House crossref rules (tests/test_manuscript_crossref.py) stay green.
- No new hand-typed empirical numbers (coordinate with 0531).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Each item fixed or explicitly waived with a one-line reason in the log.
- [ ] Manuscript builds; adherence tests green.

## Author annotation additions (reading 1, 2026-06-11)

Append to the single editorial pass:
14. Em-dashes are an AI tell — sweep and restyle (abstract and body).
15. Runs of three -ly adverbs and six-in-a-row trisyllabic words (abstract) —
    plain bad writing, simplify.
16. p2: "restrictive licences" is irrelevant to the GIGO argument — cut.
17. p2: reduce F1 prominence in the intro ("less on F1").
18. p3: define precision and recall at first use.
19. p4: clarify the Wikipedia snapshot date.
20. p4: "scaffolding" sentence is out.
21. p6: LLM-tell prose flagged near quality-bar section — rewrite plainly.
22. p6 (Figure 2 intro): remove AI contrast-framing ("not X but Y"), the
    what-it-is-not enumeration, and the unjustified opening claim that
    capability improves statistical quality — go straight to the point.
